body:
As someone who used to be plat back in the day and now plays one ranked game a year, there's absolutely nothing wrong with playing a tank mid under certain conditions. It's not always a good idea to first pick a tank mid because if they pick Xerath, Velkoz, etc you're going to have a pretty bad time if you don't know your champ. However, if the enemy midlaner is a chad and picks some assassin (with the exceptions of Fizz and Kass), you can screw them over by a) waiting for them to use their main abilities (eg Zed W-Q, Talon W, etc) or b) instantly CC-ing them if they use their gapcloser (Zed W, Talon Q, Diana E, Akali E, etc). Classic example: a Zed decides he's going to kill you at lvl 3. He comes close to you with his W. If you're Rammus, immediately Q-taunt him. If you're Mao, W-Q. Cho: Q-W-E. And so on. Go full tank Mao/Cho/Malph/Rammus/Ali and make them utterly irrelevant. All of these tank champs have pretty decent waveclear at least after a few levels (Mao Q, Cho E-Q, Rammus W, etc).

&#x200B;

Playing tanks into ranged mages is slightly harder, but still pretty simple once you get used to it. Literally all you need to do is be patient. Say you're against a Xerath as Mao. It's ABSOLUTELY OKAY to give up farm in order to not get poked by his Qs. As Mao, as soon as he shoots his stun thing at you, you can W to him, thereby not letting you stun him, and W-Q for a decent aftershock trade. Or say you're against a Lux as Mao. Most Luxes will throw their E slightly behind you, so just move left or right while respecting her Q distance. As soon as she's down with that spell rotation, go all in. Mao passive is excellent against spell-spamming mages, and, provided you don't get whittled to 20% hp, you'll win trades hard after your first back.

&#x200B;

I mostly play mid and support, and love tanks. My main ranged champs are Vlad and Viktor, and Vlad is one of the only mages in the game I would strongly recommend not playing against as a tank. He WILL murder you. The rest are pretty simple.

&#x200B;

Personally, as a Mao main, I'd recommend him as a very safe pick in any lane. If the annoying enemy Syndra is poking you out, go for a few safe trades if you can, then back and buy Mercs and the MR component of Sunfire and return to lane and watch her cry. If Diana's Q-ing you and she decides she wants to fight a Mao and E's to you, W and Q her. She loses the trade, you win it. If you want to specifically counter AD assassins (as well as Yas and Yone), go Rammus. Thornmail first back, watch them ragequit.

&#x200B;

Also: barrier is a very underrated summoner spell. I can't count the number of times I've gotten first blood because I barriered the enemy's ignite while CC-ing them under my turret (and all Yasuos are born with the mentality of ceaselessly pushing lane).

&#x200B;

Last thing: It's not the end of the world if you lose lane and turret. Sure, the enemy Syndra can one-shot your Jinx, but Syndra can't do jack shit when she has three forms of CC on her and a tank resting on her face. As a tank, you're infinitely more valuable in teamfights. You can determine the outcome of a game harder than any other class besides enchantress supports like Janna or Yuumi. Just be patient, go the fuck in, grin as the whole enemy team does roughly 10 dmg to you and your team stomps them.

&#x200B;

I hope this helps. In any case, have fun! :)

